Mechanisms (source pointers)
- crates/bboxy450-term/src/cockpit.rs:87 — bootstrap marks supervisor replacement; logic_main:307 invokes recover_seats after custodied startup, before GUI Ready. The configured supervisor-wide journal directory is preserved.
- cockpit.rs:385 — Session retains config/readiness, child control pipes, last watches and one stored recovery task. event cancellation does not discard a half-started child. Logic death replaces only logic, preserves PTYs; supervisor death reaps the old owner then replaces both. A failed recovery is named and held, rather than repeatedly advancing generations.
- cockpit.rs:441 — restoration is a finite Watch diff drained through the existing bounded writer before later UI requests. Busy, independent reader/writer tasks and owned writer_ready are preserved; event keeps draining snapshots while restoration is blocked.
- cockpit.rs:500/:578/:653 — fresh catalogue comes through existing Seats before Identity; restored watches use new view tokens and current process generation. Shutdown aborts and awaits pending/completed startup, then stops/reaps owned installed children.
- crates/bbt-mux/src/logic.rs:1302 — local/open/missing processes with confirmed running state and explicit saved launch context replay only committed predecessor state. New process generation resets capture cursor, preserves screen/parser/title/cwd/size, adds a named uncommitted-output loss gap and uses the existing launch planner for native Claude/Codex resume or fresh zsh. Natural exits clear running state. Inherited environment/capabilities are not saved.
